WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.675 --> 00:00:09.120
- Been kind of hard lately.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.120
I don't know, like, I'm super hopeful

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.890
about the future and
I'm embracing the grind.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:18.890
But sometimes it's really,
like, tiring, but...

00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:25.530
♪ Somebody asked me how I'm doing ♪

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.569
♪ And they meant it ♪

00:00:26.569 --> 00:00:28.201
♪ I don't know how to answer ♪

00:00:28.201 --> 00:00:29.719
♪ I don't know how to phrase it ♪

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:30.851
♪ And frankly, I don't know ♪

00:00:30.851 --> 00:00:32.519
♪ How I still maintain all my friendship ♪

00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:34.069
♪ 'Cause lately I've been in my head ♪

00:00:34.069 --> 00:00:35.430
♪ and kind of left it selfless ♪

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.230
- My guess is that my friends are all

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.210
just better than me. And it's a blessing

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.250
how I find a girl who's better than me.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.350
We fell in love way back
when I was someone better

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.579
than me. She's like a drug.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:46.770
The high she gives me
even better than weed.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.290
She's like a feather,
indeed. I love to carry her.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.090
She's far from a burden but I know nothing

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.280
that's heavier than my
heart when it's hurting.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.900
And all this music,
and all these endeavors

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.730
I've been working on
are just representation

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.710
of things that I've been
learning from or running from.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.378
'Cause honestly, I'm scared to death.

00:01:00.378 --> 00:01:02.490
I dropped outta school,
my life is testing me.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.770
I can't bear the stress.
I don't care for rest.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.630
I got way too many things to get to.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.950
But I realize I'm not defined

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.639
by all the things I've been through.

00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:11.040
That's all you get.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.118
Go listen to the record.

00:01:12.118 --> 00:01:14.056
(Gael laughs)

00:01:14.056 --> 00:01:16.350
- It'll be everywhere on the
screen and the description.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.290
And it's gonna be the new
intro for the series. So...

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.910
- I hope y'all connect
to the record honestly

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:21.870
and find me on Instagram.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.240
I think that's probably
one thing I look forward to

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.580
the most is connecting with
people who love my music.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.177
- I guess I'll start off by saying,

00:01:28.177 --> 00:01:29.880
"Would you like to have some tea with me?"

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.489
- Yeah! I would love to have some tea.

00:01:31.489 --> 00:01:32.610
You got some tea for me?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.590
- Here's mine. Let's do a cheers.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.200
- Oh, I keep dropping this.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.033
- That's not good.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:40.200
- Yeah, I'mma hold it. I'm okay with that.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.570
- You could clip it on.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:45.870
Have you seen my most recent
episodes on my YouTube channel?

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:46.873
I hope you haven't.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:47.706
- I have not.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:48.600
- Okay, good. That's perfect.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.580
I'm glad you haven't been watching them.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.967
So this whole series is just called,

00:01:51.967 --> 00:01:53.517
"Would you like to have some tea with me?"

00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:55.890
And the whole point is to
just to get to know you.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.540
I guess first I wanna know
how are you doing, really.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:01.890
- I'm all right, you know.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.350
I just moved to a new
town with my girlfriend.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.170
So, that's exciting but, you
know, it's also stressful.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.730
So, just dealing with that,

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.470
but I've been pretty grateful lately.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.780
Some days up, some days down as usual.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.009
- How long have you been
with your girlfriend for?

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:17.400
- It's gonna be five
years on October 30th.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.038
- Oh, wow. Congrats.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:22.200
- Thank you. Yeah, I'm
very happy about it.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.300
- Can you tell me a little
about how you guys met?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.450
- Yeah, so, we both went to Penn State

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.230
and we were both off-campus housing.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.400
And I would see her on
the bus all the time.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.710
And I lived somewhere that
was kind of far from campus.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.270
So, nobody liked to go there.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.910
So, you would only see on the
bus people that lived there.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.210
So, I saw her a while,
my second year there

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.860
and I hadn't seen her before.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.950
So, one day after a long study session,

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.367
she was on the bus alone and I was like,

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.520
"All right, this is my chance."

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.060
So I just approached her and
yeah, we started talking.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.770
She kind of ghosted me
and then two weeks later

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.792
I pointed her out to my mom.

00:02:59.792 --> 00:03:02.280
My mom came to visit and I
kind of showed her to my mom.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.710
- Like, you guys were
all on the bus together?

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.370
- Like, two weeks later.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.632
My mom came to visit and we
were about to board the bus,

00:03:07.632 --> 00:03:09.120
and I kind of tell my mom,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.020
kind of like, "Oh, this is who..."

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.390
I actually tell her in
French so I could be slick.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.010
And she turns around
and points at the girl.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:14.880
And she's like, "Oh, is it her?"

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:15.991
- Your mom?

00:03:15.991 --> 00:03:18.900
- So, there was a whole awkward situation.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.250
So, I texted her 'cause I had her number.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.990
I texted her, "Sorry about that."

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.240
And then we kind of talked again,

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.300
and then we hung out the day after that.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.490
And then five years
later we're here, yeah.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.450
- Thanks to your mom.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.560
- Yeah, straight up.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.140
My mom takes credit for it for sure, yeah.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.450
- What was her perspective,
like, on the whole thing?

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.150
Like, when she was
noticing you on the bus?

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.950
- She claims that she thought I was cute

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.270
and she noticed me. She claims.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.863
- Okay, alright. That's
all you need to know.

00:03:43.863 --> 00:03:45.660
- I mean that's five years later,

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.799
so I believe her, you know.

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:48.450
- Cool.
- Yeah.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.220
- I'm gonna go back to my
first question actually,

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.110
'cause I do want to share the story

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.790
of how you are doing, really.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.110
- Yeah.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.510
- So yesterday, me and
my cousin, we were just-

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.800
It was my only day off.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.633
- Oh wow.

00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:00.466
- Literally.

00:04:00.466 --> 00:04:01.543
- When you came in at Pata, right?

00:04:01.543 --> 00:04:03.000
- I came into Patagonia.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.770
- Yeah, that was two days ago, right?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.603
- That was two days ago, sorry.

00:04:05.603 --> 00:04:07.140
This whole trip's been a blur.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.130
- Yeah. Yeah, tell me about it.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.800
- Two days ago we were shopping.
We walked into Patagonia.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.110
My cousin found a jacket
and she wanted to get it

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:14.972
and I told her, "No, you'll
find something nicer."

00:04:14.972 --> 00:04:15.805
- Okay.

00:04:15.805 --> 00:04:16.638
- So that's why we didn't check out.

00:04:16.638 --> 00:04:17.730
We didn't meet you the first time.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:18.563
- Okay.

00:04:18.563 --> 00:04:19.650
- We didn't check out, we left.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.132
- I didn't see you guys leave
the first time, actually.

00:04:21.132 --> 00:04:21.965
- You didn't see us at all?

00:04:21.965 --> 00:04:23.280
I noticed you the first time.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.900
You were just, like, at the cashier.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.110
I noticed that you were the cashier.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.810
- Yeah, I mean, probably
that's why you saw me

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.160
'cause I was the only one at the register.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.297
- But you didn't notice me the first time?

00:04:30.297 --> 00:04:32.220
- No, I think I only saw you

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:35.040
when you guys were walking towards me.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.910
Or I think when you guys
came back the second time.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.410
- Yeah.
- I saw you guys walk by.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.520
I recognized you at
first but I wasn't sure.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.560
Then on your way down to
checkout, I heard your voice.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.930
And I was like, "Okay,
that's absolutely her."

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.698
- Everyone always says they
recognize me by my voice.

00:04:47.698 --> 00:04:49.260
- I mean you have a very particular voice.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.330
And I think, like, it's very recognizable.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.372
Like, I saw you and it didn't click fully.

00:04:53.372 --> 00:04:55.680
Yeah, when you spoke,
when I heard your voice,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.767
my heart just dropped. I was like,

00:04:56.767 --> 00:04:58.470
"Oh shit, it's definitely her."

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.020
Yeah. That's why I almost
didn't remember you.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.670
Gosh, I was like, today I
said, "Nice to meet you."

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:03.580
And she's like, "You
met me the other day."

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.680
I was like, "I'm sorry."

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.940
Listen. I wasn't like-

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:08.850
I couldn't believe what
was happening 'cuz yeah.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.380
We'll talk about this song in a second.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.020
'Cuz whatever the reason
why I knew you was

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.610
is something super important to me,

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:15.660
like, in my personal life, so.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.679
- To me, too. To me too, seriously.

00:05:16.679 --> 00:05:17.880
- Yeah. So.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:18.840
- But, let me.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.673
- Yeah. Let's tell 'em.

00:05:19.673 --> 00:05:20.738
- Sorry, I thought they
were talking to me.

00:05:20.738 --> 00:05:21.839
- Oh, me too, honestly.

00:05:21.839 --> 00:05:25.590
- But Shen, is this? You're good? Okay.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.423
Are you heading out?

00:05:26.423 --> 00:05:27.256
- [Man] Yeah.

00:05:27.256 --> 00:05:28.533
- Okay. Gimme a hug before you go.

00:05:29.609 --> 00:05:30.913
(muffled voice)

00:05:30.913 --> 00:05:32.804
- Nice meeting you, homie. Be safe, bro.

00:05:32.804 --> 00:05:33.913
- You as well.

00:05:33.913 --> 00:05:37.170
- I have these binges I do,
where I go on YouTube to cry.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.823
'Cause there's so many
amazing videos, like,

00:05:38.823 --> 00:05:41.190
like I think that's how I
would land in on the channel.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.997
'Cause I saw the, like the
question, and I was like,

00:05:42.997 --> 00:05:44.670
"Oh, I gotta see how
people react to that."

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.922
It was the, "How you doing really?" video

00:05:45.922 --> 00:05:49.740
where you were asking
strangers how they were doing

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.990
and just actually pushing
as opposed to settling

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.830
for the regular answer that we
all so used to giving people

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.886
and giving strangers. But yeah.

00:05:57.886 --> 00:06:01.050
Favorite record. Yeah.
Created because of that video.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.520
So, thank you. I guess.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.080
- Thank you. Don't thank me.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:04.977
It was the strangers.

00:06:04.977 --> 00:06:06.480
And like, it's a combination

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.160
of just people inspiring each other.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:08.993
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:10.200
- Yeah. That's why I want
to tell you the story

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.580
about my other friend,

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.340
because the record wouldn't have been...

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.320
Like, the inception was
because I was inspired

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.900
by your video, but you inspired me

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.670
and I wrote the first half.

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:21.503
- Yeah.

00:06:21.503 --> 00:06:22.336
- Which inspired him.

00:06:22.336 --> 00:06:23.169
- Right.

00:06:23.169 --> 00:06:24.077
- And seeing him be
inspired, inspired me back.

00:06:24.077 --> 00:06:25.560
- Right.
- To finish it.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:26.393
- Yeah.

00:06:26.393 --> 00:06:27.226
- Which is why it's even a record.

00:06:27.226 --> 00:06:29.400
Which is why it was even
a conversation to have.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.460
So, you know the full
circle, that's all that is.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.020
I mean.
- Teamwork.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.360
- I know, right. Unintentional teamwork.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.220
And to think about how
much it meant to me before,

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.310
I can't even explain to you
how much it means to me now.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.870
Like, even more, so.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.617
- So yeah, the first line you say,

00:06:44.617 --> 00:06:47.490
"Somebody asked me how I'm
doing and they meant it." Yeah.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.100
- Yeah. And I think, I think, yeah,

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.477
I was just going through a lot and, yeah,

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:55.200
just, like, asked myself,
I guess, how I was doing

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.280
after I saw it.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.650
And this song has been
my response to myself

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.120
and, like, struggling with the idea of,

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.970
like, being honest about how you doing

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.590
with yourself and with other people too.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.500
'Cause I believe I've written
technically better raps,

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:11.790
but it's my favorite record,
like, by far, to this day.

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.830
Yeah. And I don't listen to my music much,

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.306
but I listen to that song.

00:07:15.306 --> 00:07:16.227
- You listen to that one.

00:07:16.227 --> 00:07:17.159
- Yeah, yeah. Quite a bit. Yeah.

00:07:17.159 --> 00:07:20.850
- I do wanna tell you, like,
so you gave me the song, right?

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.338
In Patagonia. And this will be, like,

00:07:23.338 --> 00:07:26.820
probably my top 10 favorite
memories of my life.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.740
Me and Shen we went outside the Patagonia.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.470
We were sitting on this thing,
and we were waiting for Uber

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.110
and we played it. And,
like, as soon as I heard it,

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.450
I swear to God, like,
just like the first intro.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.640
Like, I was like, I like, this is so good.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:39.707
This guy's so good.

00:07:39.707 --> 00:07:40.540
- I don't believe that.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.330
- And then what you did to, like,

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.820
what happened to me when
I listened to that song

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.020
is why I do what I do.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.610
'Cause I want people to feel that.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.707
You know what I'm saying?
And so like, yeah,

00:07:49.707 --> 00:07:51.337
I ran back in there. I was like,

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.790
"I'm gonna message this guy
and I need to interview him."

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.257
