00:07:55.257 --> 00:07:58.320
it's rarely something so personal.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:00.240
Like, I feel like people will look up

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.130
to an artist because they love his music.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:04.347
But, when it's somebody
who specifically had, like,

00:08:04.347 --> 00:08:08.070
an direct effect on your
life and I think it's, like,

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.926
that's why I was so, like,
you know, like, lost in

00:08:09.926 --> 00:08:12.367
in the whole situation. It
was just like, I was like,

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:13.230
"You have to tell her."

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.348
Like, "She has to know."

00:08:14.348 --> 00:08:15.247
'Cause I was like,

00:08:15.247 --> 00:08:17.525
"Where else am I gonna
get to tell you this?"

00:08:17.525 --> 00:08:18.690
And also I was like,

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:19.847
I know you're not based here too.

00:08:19.847 --> 00:08:20.680
- Yeah.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:21.660
- That was crazy.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.006
- So, I was gonna ask you
what's a line in that song

00:08:24.006 --> 00:08:26.160
